    "country_code": "USA",
    "description": "Amazon Leo is an initiative to launch a constellation of Low Earth Orbit satellites that will provide low-latency, high-speed broadband network connectivity to unserved and underserved communities around the world - from individual households to schools, hospitals, businesses, and government agencies.<br/><br/>Export Control Requirement:<br/>Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum.<br/><br/><br/>Key job responsibilities<br/>- Design and implement globally available distributed cloud architectures<br/>- Actively participate in overall technical strategy and charter expansion<br/>- Design core ETL framework capabilities shaping data from 50+ producers to be accessed by dozens of consumers<br/>- Own the schema evolution system across Iceberg, Glue registry, and DataZone, enforcing platform patterns.<br/>- Solve novel problems at the intersection of AI, distributed systems, and financial domain complexity<br/>- Define reference architectures, templates, blueprints, infrastructure standards, and data quality frameworks for domain teams.<br/>- Partner with domain and consumer teams across Amazon Leo Commerce, Networking, and Satellite teams.<br/>- Own operational excellence for their components: monitoring, alarming, DLQ/retry, and incident root-cause analysis.<br/><br/>A day in the life<br/>Have you wanted an opportunity to develop the software applications and services for an advanced global communications service? This role is for a Software Development Engineer who will design, build, and maintain components and services of Leo Commerce Services.<br/><br/>About the team<br/>This position is for the Data Platform team, which sits within the Amazon Leo Commerce organization. We're part of the exciting Amazon Leo initiative - Amazon's effort to provide global broadband connectivity - and our corner of that world focuses on the commerce experience.<br/><br/>What does Leo Commerce do? <br/>Simply put, we build the services and applications that help Leo customers discover, purchase, and use Leo connectivity services and products. Think of us as the part of Leo behind the customer-facing website and all the features that make the business side of Leo actually work.<br/><br/>What does Data Platform specifically own? <br/>We're the data folks! We build and maintain the tools that propagate and store data from all Leo Commerce systems. This means enabling teams across the org to query data, generate reports, and unlock business insights that drive real decisions. This means we have the important role of understanding the big picture of Leo Commerce systems. We also have recently took on owning SOX Compliance, since financial data fits well within our data charter.<br/><br/>But here's the thing: while \"Data Platform\" is our name, we're proudly cross-functional engineers. You might see your teammates automating User Acceptance Testing (UAT) for our retail websites, implementing features to ensure proper data handling for Accounting, or jumping into whatever challenge needs solving. We're owners in the truest sense: if it helps get Amazon Leo to launch, we're all in.",
